{"id": "EUVD-2026-80534", "enisaUuid": "c4024054-2199-3fb5-a53b-2fa69cbfd384", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: light: ltrf216a: fix runtime PM reference leak in error path\n\nltrf216a_get_lux() acquires a runtime PM reference by calling\nltrf216a_set_power_state(data, true). However, if\nltrf216a_read_data() fails, the function returns immediately without\ndropping the reference.\n\nThis leaves the runtime PM usage count unbalanced, preventing the device\nfrom autosuspending after a failed read.\n\nFix this by releasing the runtime PM reference before returning from the\nerror path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4bf5525c6ff4a9f8df35bcc227a918b6396b2cb5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c4f003d8578f5718fe1ec332bc89f9ff69fd205b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0614928a3eda35bddd8c2f02311e286b59bbe746", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/80e7381e8cccb543397572af153865f34aaf4353", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c132aef0e757a39036b1d40faf0569f2e343b13e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jq92-qr7r-j3m3", "CVE-2026-89934"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "016c5467-30a0-3144-a7a7-150b6652e17b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "83f0bcd40d5cf88870d2f2bb8b97c772b92a3d1f <4bf5525c6ff4a9f8df35bcc227a918b6396b2cb5"}, {"id": "04dd1201-63b6-3da7-bcc8-ceb244dd98fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "83f0bcd40d5cf88870d2f2bb8b97c772b92a3d1f <0614928a3eda35bddd8c2f02311e286b59bbe746"}, {"id": "04ef2ae6-3f9f-3462-a20a-c8334e8cd7c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "08c2a92c-7f20-34ce-b227-7baaaf27fddb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "83f0bcd40d5cf88870d2f2bb8b97c772b92a3d1f <c4f003d8578f